      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larson%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Its early success came from the railroad right‑of‑way that supplied goods to settlers in Keller, Forthun, and surrounding townships.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larson%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Both Larson and nearby Columbus were named for Columbus Larson, an early postmaster who served the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larson%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Larson’s city government was dissolved in 2003, officially ending its municipal status.",
